  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Reviewing UI Goals**\n\nI\'m focusing now on the user interface\'s final form. I\'m prioritizing the interactive dashboard concept for project navigation, keeping in mind the digital learning playbook for students new to robotics that was requested.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have completed the Robotics Playbook, designing a vibrant, interactive \"Doodle Pop\" web application tailored for students.\n\nHere is a summary of the implementation:\n- **Doodle Pop Aesthetic**: Created a playful, high-contrast visual identity featuring thick black outlines, bold offset drop-shadows, and a dotted notebook canvas. Typography is driven by `Shantell Sans` to give it an authentic, hand-drawn marker feel.\n- **Interactive Dashboard**: Designed a landing hub where students can track their progress, featuring an unlocked introductory Chapter 1 and visually locked future chapters.\n- **Chapter 1 (\"The Spark of Life!\")**: Structured the complete first lesson with focused, single-view pedagogical sections:\n  - **Basic Principles**: Simple, visual explanations of Voltage, Current, and Resistance.\n  - **Parts List**: A visual inventory of the Arduino Uno, LED, Resistors, and Breadboard using clear iconography.\n  - **Math & Physics**: An approachable breakdown of Ohm\'s Law calculating the correct resistor limit for an LED.\n  - **Wiring Diagram**: Implemented a custom inline SVG line-doodle mapping the circuit connections.\n  - **Code**: A dark-themed snippet editor showcasing the Arduino `blink.ino` C++ sketch.\n  - **Independent Exercises**: Fun standalone challenges designed to reinforce learning, including speeding up the blink rate, creating an S.O.S. pattern, and adding a secondary \"police light.\""
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 1
      nanos: 819351857
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
